{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_adr", "label": "ADR 0004: ddrop dashboard binds a TCP port and is a control-socket client", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Status accepted. Exists because a browser cannot open a Unix socket, so a dashboard appears to conflict head-on with ADR 0003 and invariant 3."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "label": "ddrop dashboard command", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 13-21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Binds an HTTP server on 127.0.0.1 serving a static page plus a read-only JSON API, and reaches the runtime as a client of the control socket exactly as ddrop status does. It constructs no DeadDropRuntime, so only ddrop start and ddrop connect remain runtime constructors."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_read_only_constraint", "label": "Read-only constraint on the dashboard API", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 18, 27-29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No route publishes, calls, exposes, cancels or retries, and the socket's write routes (/publish, /call, /expose) are not proxied. Read-only is what preserves the argument that the browser user already holds this capability by being able to run ddrop status, so it is a constraint of the decision and not a first-release simplification."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_control_socket_client", "label": "Dashboard as another control-socket consumer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The control plane is unchanged: still a socket at mode 0600, with the dashboard in the same category as ddrop status, ddrop discover and ddrop logs. Nothing about the runtime's listener moves."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_control_plane_routes", "label": "Structured control-plane data (/peers, /transports, /status, /queues, logs, traces, metrics)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything a read-only dashboard would show already exists here, which is why the dashboard needs no runtime of its own and can show nothing the control plane does not already return."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_loopback_bind", "label": "Explicit 127.0.0.1 bind, never 0.0.0.0", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 19, 48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The port is a view of data the operator can already read in their own terminal, held open by a foreground process that exits when they stop it."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_browser_reachable_threat", "label": "Browser-reachable localhost threat (CSRF, Origin, DNS rebinding)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The decisive reason is narrower than 'TCP is riskier than a socket' and specific to browsers: any web page the user visits can issue requests at 127.0.0.1. Defending state-changing endpoints needs Origin validation, CSRF tokens and DNS-rebinding-resistant Host checks, each easy and collectively easy to get subtly wrong. When every endpoint only reads, the worst outcome degrades from an action taken to information disclosed."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_writable_dashboard_reopens_adr", "label": "A writable dashboard would reopen this ADR", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A cancel or retry button is two stacked decisions: whether to build a job-control primitive at all (nothing in the runtime cancels a queued message today, and redelivery is already automatic), and whether to put it on a browser-reachable port. Keep them apart."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_idempotencykey_retry_hazard", "label": "Request-level retry hazard under at-least-once delivery", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Delivery is at-least-once and idempotencyKey dedupes per runtime only, so retrying onto a second worker runs the job twice with neither side able to notice, and no backend offers the compare-and-swap needed to fix that."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_no_runtime_construction", "label": "Dashboard constructs no DeadDropRuntime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 13, 21, 33-39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The second half of the decision matters more than the TCP question, because the tempting implementation (copy ddrop connect) is the wrong one. A dashboard that only reads needs no runtime, no workDir, no peer id and no beacons. The general rule the workDir bugs taught: dead-drop's own machinery must not entangle itself with the thing the user is sharing."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_workdir_ownership", "label": "workDir ownership collision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A git working tree has one writer. The ownership lock added in 0.2.5 catches the second runtime and forces it into <workDir>.peers/, so every dashboard session would clone the whole data branch."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_phantom_peers", "label": "Phantom peers from ephemeral client identities", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A runtime publishes presence beacons under an ephemeral <configured>-c<pid-hex> identity, so every dashboard session would appear in every peer's ddrop discover as a peer that answers nothing."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_unbounded_commits", "label": "Unbounded beacon commits on git and github", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On the git and github transports each beacon is a commit and a push, so a dashboard left open all day would write commits all day into a history that already grows without bound."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_explicit_port_policy", "label": "Explicit --port with loud EADDRINUSE failure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults to a port ddrop connect does not hand out and fails loudly rather than hunting for a free one, because a dashboard that silently moves is a dashboard nobody can bookmark."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_metadata_disclosure", "label": "Workspace metadata disclosure through the open port", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Peer names, channel names, queue depths, and through logs and traces rather more, are readable by anything with local access while the port is open. The names are already in the clear in the store's object keys (invariant 9), but that store is readable by workspace members whereas this port is readable by any process on the machine and by content the user's browser loads. A smaller audience shift than a write capability, still a real one, so the port is loopback-bound, open only during the foreground command, and documented as carrying workspace metadata."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_browser_open_optional", "label": "Opening a browser is a convenience, not a dependency", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The URL is printed before the open is attempted, --no-open skips it, and a failed open never fails the command, because dead-drop runs on headless machines as an ordinary deployment where open fails or hangs."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_retention_store", "label": "Retention store for completed jobs (deferred)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Completed jobs and who requested them' cannot be shown because delivery is delete-as-acknowledgement and no record of a finished job survives. Keeping one changes what the runtime retains and therefore touches the security model, so it is a separate decision."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_serve_from_runtime_rejected", "label": "Serve the dashboard from the runtime itself (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The shortest path and the worst one: it puts a TCP listener on the process holding the secrets, exactly what ADR 0003 forbids, and makes every ddrop start a web server whether or not anyone wants one."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_top_rejected", "label": "Terminal UI ddrop top (rejected as a substitute)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Genuinely appealing, needs no port, still worth building on its own merits, but not a substitute: the ask was something to leave open on a second monitor and hand to someone who does not use the CLI."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_cdn_frontend_rejected", "label": "Load the frontend library from a CDN (rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rejected on principle: the product exists to work through infrastructure you already have, sometimes offline, so a dashboard needing the internet to render contradicts it. The library is vendored into the CLI package's static assets, keeping it out of the dependency tree and leaving the zero-runtime-dependency claim intact."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_vendored_assets", "label": "Vendored static frontend assets in the CLI package", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vendoring keeps the frontend out of the dependency tree and preserves the zero-runtime-dependency claim while allowing offline rendering."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_invariant_3", "label": "Invariant 3: control plane is a socket or named pipe, never TCP", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The repository invariant that encodes ADR 0003 and that the dashboard appears to violate at a glance."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_invariant_9", "label": "Invariant 9: names are in the clear in store object keys", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Peer and channel names are already visible to workspace members in object keys; the dashboard port widens the audience for that same metadata to any local process."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_connect", "label": "ddrop connect (runtime constructor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 21, 33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Builds a DeadDropRuntime from the user's config. Copying it into the dashboard would import all three of its collisions with whatever the user is sharing."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_status", "label": "ddrop status (existing control-socket client)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 13, 17, 27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The precedent the dashboard is modelled on, and the capability baseline the read-only argument rests on."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_adr", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_invariant_3", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_invariant_3", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 13", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_control_socket_client", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 13, 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_control_socket_client", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_unix_domain_socket", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_status", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 13, 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_read_only_constraint", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 18", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_loopback_bind", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 19", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_ddrop_dashboard", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_control_plane_routes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 7, 50", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_browser_reachable_threat", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_read_only_constraint", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_browser_reachable_threat", "target": "docs_adr_0003_unix_socket_control_plane_localhost_tcp_rejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "lines 25, 29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_writable_dashboard_reopens_adr", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_read_only_constraint", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0004-dashboard-binds-tcp-and-holds-no-runtime.md", "source_location": "line 31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_idempotencykey_retry_hazard", "target": "docs_adr_0004_dashboard_binds_tcp_and_holds_no_runtime_writable_dashboard_reop